Calculate the entropy change (J/mol K) of the given reaction. The molar entropies [J/K mol] are given in brackets after each substance.

\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} [91.2] + 3 \text{O}_2(g) [205.1] \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} [66.5] + 2 \text{SO}_2(g) [248.2] \]<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","Here here how to calculate the change in entropy (ΔS) for the reaction:

**1.  Calculate the total entropy of the products:**

*  2 *  PbO(s) * 66.5 J/ K mol = 133.0 J/ K mol
*  2 * SO₂(g) * 248.2 J/ K mol = 496.4 J/ K mol
*  Total entropy of products = 133.0 + 496.4 = 569.4 J/ K mol

**2. Calculate the total entropy of the reactants:**

* 2 * PbS(s) * 91.2 J/ K mol = 122.4 J/ K mol
* 3 * O₂(g) * 205.1 J/ K mol = 615.3 J/ K mol
* Total entropy of reactants = 122.4 + 615.3 = 737.7 J/ K mol

**3. Calculate the change in entropy: **

ΔS = (Total entropy of products) - (Total entropy of reactants)

ΔS = 569.4 J/ K mol - 737.7 J/ K mol = -167.3 J/ K mol


 
**Therefore, the change in entropy for the reaction is -167.3 J/ K mol.** 


