A **sorption isotherm** is a graphical representation of the amount of a substance (the **sorate) that is adsorbed onto a surface (the sorbent) at a specific temperature and pressure.** It plots the amount of the sorate adsorbed per gram of the sorbent (or other unit of the sorbent) as the concentration of the solate in the surrounding solution (or gas) changes.

