    *  ΔS<sub>g</sub> = 1 kg * 1.005 kJ/ kgK * ln(823/1473) = -0.64 kJ/ K

**3. Calculate the change in entropy of the water:**

*  The change in entropy of the water is:
    *  ΔS<sub>w</sub> = m * (ΔH/T)
    where:
    * m = mass of the water (1 kg)
    * ΔH = latent heat of vaporization (1858.5 kJ/ kg)
    * T = temperature of the vaporization (220°C = 293 K)

*  Therefore, ΔS<sub>w</sub> = 1 kg * (1858.5 kJ/ kg) / 293 K = 6.56 kJ/ K

